  YM: {
    label:"YM", unit:"pt", dp:0, seed:53668.0,
    sub:"",
    levels:[
      { p:54320.0, name:"Window high", st:"untested", tests:0,
        why:"The top of the 510.2-hour window on 0.09% of window volume. Nothing above this has ever traded inside the measurement, so the correct output above it is UNMAPPED rather than clear air." },
      { p:54150.44, name:"The thirty-four-turn cash-made cluster", st:"held", tests:34,
        why:"Thirty-four turns — sixteen in the US cash session, thirteen European, four Asian and one in the evening — scored 36 on 0.74% of window volume. Stale at about 347 hours. The model calls its side above and grades it reachable inside a cash session at an excursion multiple of 14.6." },
      { p:54020.0, name:"Value-area high", st:"held", tests:75,
        why:"Upper edge of the 70% value area across the whole window, on 2.50% of window volume. 86.76% of everything traded in the window happened at or below this price, so it is the boundary value has reached rather than a shelf the market built." },
      { p:53880.19, name:"The eighty-eight-turn Asian cluster", st:"held", tests:88,
        why:"Eighty-eight turns — forty-three Asian, twenty-six in the US cash session, sixteen European and three in the evening — scored 71 on 1.89% of window volume, and the third-heaviest pool on this board. Stale at about 319 hours. The model calls its side above and grades it reachable inside a cash session at an excursion multiple of 6.4." },
      { p:53702.66, name:"The seventy-one-turn Asian cluster", st:"held", tests:71,
        why:"Seventy-one turns — twenty-nine Asian, twenty in the US cash session, twenty European and two in the evening — scored 81 on 1.55% of window volume, and the second-heaviest pool on this board. Set about eight hours before the snapshot. The model calls its side above and grades it reachable inside a session at an excursion multiple of 1.1." },
      { p:53500.0, name:"POC — the magnet", st:"held", tests:112,
        why:"Point of control: more contracts changed hands in this 20-point bin than in any other across 510.2 hours, 4.25% of window volume. The eleven bins around it hold 31.27% of everything traded between them, so this is a neighbourhood rather than a line." },
      { p:53360.0, name:"Value-area low", st:"untested", tests:0,
        why:"Lower edge of the 70% value area across the whole window, on 1.01% of window volume, with 83.75% of everything traded at or above it. Thin, which is what makes it a boundary rather than a shelf." },
      { p:53200.0, name:"The best bid in the twenty-nine-bin void", st:"untested", tests:0,
        why:"The heaviest bin in a twenty-nine-bin void running 52,800 to 53,360 — all of those bins together hold 17.26% of everything traded, an average of 0.60% each. This one carries 1.11% of window volume, and that is the most a retrace has to catch on anywhere inside the stretch." },
      { p:52800.0, name:"Window low", st:"untested", tests:0,
